# secrets — never commit
#
# Ignore every .env variant, then allow the one that is meant to be shared.
# The previous patterns had two gaps that mattered: `.env*.local` requires the name
# to END in .local, so `.env.local.backup` was NOT ignored; and `.vercel` further
# down matches the directory, not the file `.env.vercel` that `vercel env pull`
# writes. Both were sitting untracked-but-stageable — one `git add -A` from being
# committed. Prefix matching closes that class of gap for good.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# API keys pasted into files. Generic, so a new one is covered without an edit.
*_key.txt
*_key.json
*.pem
*credentials*.json

# dependencies
node_modules/

# next.js
.next/
out/
build/
next-env.d.ts

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.log*

# TypeScript incremental build cache
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vercel
